Ohle Claussen wrote:

> Yes. So you need approx. 1 tripe per shop.

Umm, maybe.

I've decided [without bothering to do the source
code analysis and very hard math, so I may well be
wrong], that feeding pets a tripe ration or two to
promote apporting is another devteam trap, something
that looks good only if you don't look at it too
hard.

Apporting tendency in the pet from being rewarded
with a treat wears out, and fairly fast, on a
per-robbery basis, but a pet hovering around the PC
hoping to be rewarded with a PC-carried treat the
pet detects doesn't.

Rewarding the pet with tripe doesn't seem to be
nearly as effective long term (over several shops,
or several time-separated robberies of one shop) as
is holding onto that one and only tripe ration
"forever" and just taking advantage of the pets'
modest tendency to hover nearer a PC carrying a
treat.

You'd better have a good supply of food to choose
this tactic, though.

YMMV

